WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.290
- But you left college
to make YouTube videos,

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:05.490
so exactly how excited were
your parents about this?

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.350
- They were, they were the ones
that actually encouraged me

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.810
to, like, pursue my dreams
and move out to L.A., so--

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:10.643
- Whoa.
- I know, right?

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.050
I had the blessing of a brown parent,

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:13.650
you know that don't happen every day, no.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.767
(audience clapping)

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.730
- Blessing of a brown--
- I did, I did.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.230
So, my dad and my mom actually

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.650
met in theater class in college

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:23.440
and my dad was told he would only be,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.040
like, stereotype-cast as a brown man.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.770
And so, now here I am, bein' a brown girl

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.570
doin' all the things--
- Oh, that's why.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.403
- I'm doin' it for him.

00:00:31.403 --> 00:00:33.193
- That's why you're for you, yes.

00:00:33.193 --> 00:00:34.483
- I'm so proud to represent.

00:00:34.483 --> 00:00:35.793
- That's so cool and
that's where you must get

00:00:35.793 --> 00:00:38.090
your talent from, that
both of them are like, wow.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:38.923
- Yeah, that's what they like to say.

00:00:38.923 --> 00:00:40.799
My sister says I stole her personality--

00:00:40.799 --> 00:00:43.860
- (laughs) My sister and I are identical,

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.494
so I didn't steal anything, Lisa.

00:00:45.494 --> 00:00:47.810
So, who's like your favorite person

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.610
you've ever had on your YouTube channel?

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:53.360
- Um, lucky enough, I had Barack Obama,

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.237
President Barack Obama,
on my YouTube channel.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:58.303
- Wow.
- I know.

00:00:58.303 --> 00:01:01.040
He's big into the YouTube.
- That's amazing.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.500
- Yeah, it was--
- What was that like?

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.200
Were you nervous?
- Oh, so nervous.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.970
The man walked into the
room, he smelled like

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:08.065
all types of pumpkin spice
fall candles, like, he,

00:01:08.065 --> 00:01:09.570
(laughing)

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.780
every candle, every
dryer sheet known to man,

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.670
that's what he smells like.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:14.880
- Oh my gosh.
- Did he play himself?

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.190
- He played himself.
- 'Cause I was gonna say,

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.160
I would love to see him
playing something else.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.821
- He played the President and
he did the role really well.

00:01:19.821 --> 00:01:22.354
- Yes, imagine that.
- Yeah, yeah. (laughs)

00:01:22.354 --> 00:01:24.546
(audience clapping)

00:01:24.546 --> 00:01:27.471
- Try clapping now.
- Yes, I'm clapping now.

